n in kent  uh other countries acted almost  immediately to ban  travel from the uk why are we treating  it differently  so the uk has uh carried out the genome  sequencing  of uh nearly half of the entire world's  coronavirus  knowledge if you like so uh we're the  sort of the world's leading  uh country when it comes to that genome  sequencing and you do have to go through  the sequencing to understand  what the what the virus is is doing so  um we we were able with the kent variant  to tell the world straight away this is  exactly what it is  this is what it looks like we've we've  sequenced it  and as soon as we did that we provided  the information to the who  and told other countries um so this is a  bit different this is a this is a  variant from somewhere else  and say there have been thousands of  different variants and takes a little  bit of time to  uh to test that in the meantime everyone  will have had to  quarantine and in any case uh they don't  there weren't direct flights coming from  brazil so  you're saying other countries sorry to  interrupt you're saying that other  countries acted  uh more quickly because we clearly  identified the variant whereas  the variant from brazil hasn't been  clearly identified to you  right so we do a lot of the work in our  own labs um as we did with the south  african variant so to take that one as  an example  um we knew about the variant south  africa knew about the variant  we then got samples of it brought back  to uh to the uk i think to put them down  and then did the analysis uh and uh that  that analysis  um takes days and weeks rather than  hours um to do  but as i say there haven't been flights  coming from brazil in the meantime we've  acted extremely  uh quickly and our scientists aren't  saying that the vaccine won't work  against it  we just want to you know we're at this  late stage now we've we've got so far  we've  got jabs into the arms of three million  uh brits now that's more than france  spain  