y remember that this is actually  um a secondary thing the test because  the first thing is the quarantine which  is required already  and is by law already in place and has  been for a very very long time  but the issue is there are over 200  countries and territories they all have  different types of corona tests  we need to be able to advise accurately  which test people should be able to  must take before they come to the uk and  what we didn't want to do is create a  secondary crisis a repatriation crisis a  brits trying to return  home unsure whether tests in the  particular location they happen to be  uh would be sufficient uh to allow uh  for their  re-entry so uh just for practical  uh for practical purposes to make sure  that brits can return home  uh we've we've provided a little bit of  grace  but everybody coming from anywhere not  on travel corridor  must by law quarantine and there are no  exceptions um to that  and you can end up with a criminal  record if you don't  just to clarify uh just going back um if  i may  with the french border issue are they  not  requiring pcr tests no they do require  pcr tests for uh  people visiting so i think this is where  the confusions come in and by the way  we're in a lockdown nobody should be  moving nobody should be visiting uh in  any case we don't we're not encouraging  uk citizens or anyone in the uk to start  moving around  nationally or internationally but in  addition to that we have this  arrangement with regard to hauliers so  this is so that our goods and services  our food and medicine can carry on  flowing uh across to uh calais and in  that case  um they are able to take uh what are  called lateral flow tests the advantage  being that the test results come within  about 30 minutes  uh and that situation is unchanged in  fact we're welcoming  a delegation from france to the uk today  to actually  um study how we put this process in  place as i say it's the world's biggest  testing of of lorry drivers anywhere in  the world we've done over 66  000 of these tests and we've got a lot  of expertise which they're actually  coming to have a look at today  so british haulers will be totally  unaffected  well i should one thing i should say is  actually 85 percent of julia's  who ply that route are actually european  haulers  so the vast majority are not british  haulers we're mostly  testing actually european haulers in  this particular case  but for the time being there's there's  no change i can't promise what will  happen forever  and a day but um viewers will have  noticed or probably recalled those  scenes of kent being full of lorries  nothing to do with brexit but simply  because  uh the french decided to close their  border  uh when they heard about that uk variant  which is called b117  and uh but we then put this testing in  place that reopened the border and  there'd been no cues  and no disruption uh either through um  the  the covert testing or even indeed the  new paperwork that's uh that's come in  uh at the borders in this last couple of  weeks since that's happened  and we look forward to continuing to see  a smooth operation  down in kent as well grant chaps thank  you very much for  speaking to us this morning

